        <mxCell id="s1-note" parent="1" style="shape=note;size=14;fillColor=#e0e0e0;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;fontSize=9;align=left;spacingLeft=5;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap" value="SECTION 1 DATA FLOW:&#xa;1. go build reads go.mod, resolves modules from proxy&#xa;2. compile tool compiles each .go → .a (archive)&#xa;3. link tool links all .a files → final binary&#xa;4. All dependencies statically compiled into binary&#xa;&#xa;Key: Go has no dynamic linking by default&#xa;All modules + stdlib are statically linked&#xa;&#xa;Go Build Tools:&#xa;• go build — the only build command&#xa;• compile, link — internal tools (in GOTOOLDIR)&#xa;• No separate package manager — go mod is built-in" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="175" width="253" x="577" y="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
